          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "`SelfBinaryTransplantPort` restates upstream behavior in its entry and method docs: copying the running binary, byte identity, execute-permission preservation, and fail-closed failure modes are all IN/CN/AC contract text. Per `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md`, the catalogue should describe the target/operation and cite anchors, not duplicate the behavior contract in prose.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/template-export-sotp-binary-transplant-2026-07-08/usecase-types.json",
              "line": 88,
              "category": "SoT integrity: upstream restatement"
            },
            {
              "message": "`FsSelfBinaryTransplantAdapter` restates the spec contract in the adapter docs, including `current_exe`, byte-identical copy, execute permission, and fail-closed error behavior. That makes the infrastructure catalogue a second prose owner of IN-01/CN-01/CN-02/CN-06/AC-03; reduce this to adapter target + port implementation + anchor cites per the no-upstream-restatement convention.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/template-export-sotp-binary-transplant-2026-07-08/infrastructure-types.json",
              "line": 38,
              "category": "SoT integrity: upstream restatement"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:6ec272dc592f5ce5e9b7041b801917049db5bf52899b36c22341024c6eae853c",
          "at": "2026-07-08T07:55:25Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "`SelfBinaryTransplantError`'s `docs` field restates the upstream fail-closed behavior in prose, including the path-resolution/write/permission stages and the export non-zero outcome. The types severity policy treats upstream restatement in `<layer>-types.json` docs as a SoT-integrity issue; this should be reduced to the changed type plus anchor cites per `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md`.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/template-export-sotp-binary-transplant-2026-07-08/usecase-types.json",
              "line": 241,
              "category": "SoT integrity"
            },
            {
              "message": "`TemplateExportError`'s `docs` field repeats behavioral rationale for `BinaryTransplant` and fail-closed driver rendering instead of just declaring the added variant and citing the relevant anchors. That duplicates upstream behavior text in the catalogue contract, contrary to `knowledge/conventions/no-upstream-restatement.md`.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/template-export-sotp-binary-transplant-2026-07-08/usecase-types.json",
              "line": 363,
              "category": "SoT integrity"
            },
            {
              "message": "`TemplateExportInteractor` declares a modified `new` constructor with a third `transplant_port` parameter, but the entry docs say the impl surface is byte-stable and that only the private field set widens. The catalogue is internally inconsistent about whether this is a public constructor API change, which can mislead Phase 3 implementation/review. Update the entry to acknowledge the constructor signature change.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/template-export-sotp-binary-transplant-2026-07-08/usecase-types.json",
              "line": 440,
              "category": "SoT integrity"
            },
            {
              "message": "The reference entries for `TemplateExportPort` and `TemplateExportPortError` cite `IN-02`, but `IN-02` is the self-binary transplant fail-closed contract. These baseline filesystem-export entries neither perform the transplant nor construct `SelfBinaryTransplantError`, so the anchor is off-topic and creates a false catalogue-to-spec edge. Drop `IN-02` from those reference entries or replace it with an anchor that actually supports the baseline export edge.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "track/items/template-export-sotp-binary-transplant-2026-07-08/usecase-types.json",
              "line": 187,
              "category": "SoT integrity"
            }
          ],
